<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Māhele</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848</span> · Also known as Great Mahele</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Māhele was the land division of 1848 in the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, carried out under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-iii">Kamehameha III</a>. It divided the land, previously held under the chiefs, among the crown, the government and the chiefs, and later laws allowed commoners and, from 1850, foreigners to own land outright. Within decades much land had passed to foreign, mainly American, owners and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-mahele.jpg" alt="Great Māhele" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kalama, Simona P.; Lahainaluna Seminary · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Na_mokupuni_o_Hawaii_nei_LOC_98680907.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
